# Go Backend Standards

## Framework
- Use Go with Gin.
- Follow idiomatic Go conventions.
- Use the standard library where practical.
- Use GORM for database access.
- Use golang-migrate for schema migrations.

## Project Structure

Follow the existing structure:

- cmd/: application entry points.
- internal/: private application implementation.
- internal/modules/: business modules.
- internal/platform/: infrastructure.
- migrations/: database migrations.

## Coding Standards

- Use meaningful package and variable names.
- Handle errors explicitly.
- Avoid unnecessary interfaces.
- Avoid global mutable state.
- Use context.Context for cancellation.
- Pass dependencies explicitly.
- Keep functions focused.

## HTTP Layer

Handlers must:
- Parse and validate requests.
- Invoke application services.
- Return consistent responses.
- Avoid embedding business logic.

## Database

- Use transactions for multi-step operations.
- Define explicit constraints.
- Avoid N+1 queries.
- Use indexes appropriately.
- Never rely exclusively on ORM auto-migration.

## API

- Use /api/v1 versioning.
- Return appropriate HTTP status codes.
- Implement pagination for collections.
- Use consistent error responses.

## Testing

- Use Go testing package.
- Test business logic independently.
- Add integration tests for database operations.
- Mock external dependencies when appropriate.